# Voting (Nuxt 3)

Read [docs/apps/voting.md](../../docs/apps/voting.md) first.

## Layout

- `pages/` — file-based routes
- `layouts/` — `default` (constrained main) and `fullwidth` (login)
- `stores/` — Pinia stores (`auth`, `language`, `project`)
- `composables/` — shared Vue composables
- `middleware/` — global `auth.global.ts`
- `components/` — Vue SFCs (registration-style shell: `AppHeader`, `AppFooter`, `CtaButton`, etc.)
- `nuxt.config.ts` — Nuxt config

## Stack

- Nuxt 3, Vue 3, TypeScript (ESM)
- Tailwind CSS (`@nuxtjs/tailwindcss`) — same tokens as registration (`primary` `#00AEA9`)
- Pinia with `@pinia/nuxt` and persisted state (`@pinia-plugin-persistedstate/nuxt`)
- Vitest for tests (`npm run test --workspace=apps/voting`)

## API

- SPA mode (`ssr: false` in `nuxt.config.ts`)
- API base URL: `runtimeConfig.public.apiBaseURL` from `NUXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`
- Voting endpoints on API root (`/auth/login`, `/projects`, etc.) — see `VotingController`
- Jury auth: username/password → JWT Bearer in Pinia (not cookie session like registration)
- Do **not** import `@coolestprojects/database`

## Conventions

- Use Pinia stores for client state that persists across routes
- Call API via `useApiClient` / `useApiFetch` — keep pages thin
- Notifications via `useNotification` + `AppNotification` (not Nuxt UI toasts)
- Dev port 3005 in Dev Container; proxy at `voting.coolestprojects.localhost`

## Tests

- Vitest; colocate tests near the code they cover
